  "description": "DAFGUO crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H72 Dy8 N24 O28 4+,2(Cl1 1-),18(H2 O1),18(C1 H4 O1),2(H1 O1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.718-3.856 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.08-109.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy8(OH)8(phendox)6(H2O)8]Cl2(OH)2·18H2O·18MeOH (C102H170Cl2N24O66Dy8). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
